WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:05.270
The semifinal match between Satoshi and Shota at the Kalos League Miare Tournament...

00:01.980 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:06.180 --> 00:09.920
...ended with a victory for Satoshi after what had been a fierce fight for both of them.

00:10.840 --> 00:13.060
And now, his opponent in the finals is Alan.

00:13.840 --> 00:19.090
With the battle being tomorrow, what are Satoshi and Alan's thoughts?

00:23.600 --> 00:26.380
Your Pokémon have all recovered.

00:26.560 --> 00:28.180
Thank you very much, Joy-san.

00:30.700 --> 00:31.630
Welcome back, Pikachu!

00:33.670 --> 00:34.180
Do your best...

00:34.710 --> 00:35.640
...in the finals!

00:36.360 --> 00:37.960
Yes, I will!

00:39.460 --> 00:39.820
Yo,

00:41.370 --> 00:42.150
Satoshi-kun!

00:42.660 --> 00:43.180
Satoshi-san!

00:43.870 --> 00:45.720
Limone-san! Citroid!

00:47.760 --> 00:48.860
I see, I see.

00:49.590 --> 00:51.120
This will make me receive EXP.

00:51.370 --> 00:52.300
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:53.720 --> 00:54.600
Papa!

00:55.130 --> 00:56.400
What is the matter?

00:58.120 --> 01:02.370
I brought snacks to help you get ready for tomorrow's finals!

01:02.980 --> 01:03.440
Whoa!

01:03.440 --> 01:04.990
Wow, they looks delicious!

01:05.740 --> 01:07.080
Those are Miare Galettes!

01:07.840 --> 01:10.590
They're very popular and incredibly hard to get ahold of!

01:11.180 --> 01:12.790
Papa, you're awesome!

01:13.640 --> 01:15.430
Nah, you're exaggerating...

01:15.430 --> 01:17.540
I stood in line alone!

01:19.680 --> 01:21.390
Waiting for 120 minutes is no big deal to me!

01:22.490 --> 01:23.890
That can't have been fun.

01:24.480 --> 01:25.290
It was nothing.

01:25.720 --> 01:28.440
Reminding myself that it was for you guys made it an easy feat.

01:29.000 --> 01:31.020
That is my line.

01:32.340 --> 01:33.840
Come on, eat up!

01:33.840 --> 01:34.530
Yay!

01:35.100 --> 01:36.510
Everyone, come out!

01:44.380 --> 01:45.280
You too!

01:49.390 --> 01:50.210
Please come out!

02:01.140 --> 02:02.120
So good!

02:04.880 --> 02:05.940
They're tasty, right?

02:11.510 --> 02:12.700
Isn't this great?

02:12.700 --> 02:13.520
Delicious!

02:13.920 --> 02:15.810
The sugar is soaking into my brain!

02:16.140 --> 02:17.970
Shota, you love sweets, don't you?

02:18.740 --> 02:19.110
Yes!

02:20.710 --> 02:24.460
Guys, eat these and make sure to give me another passionate battle tomorrow! Don't let me down now!

02:27.660 --> 02:28.280
Satoshi,

02:28.600 --> 02:31.640
please do your best in the finals tomorrow. I will be rooting for you.

02:31.920 --> 02:33.340
I will. Thank you.

02:57.200 --> 03:02.950
Fierce Fighting at the Kalos League!
Gather, All of My Passion!!

03:12.030 --> 03:21.930
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

03:12.030 --> 03:21.930
Z

03:38.350 --> 03:40.250
Which one should I choose?

03:41.490 --> 03:44.100
If you have this one, your wish will come true.

03:44.520 --> 03:45.700
This will be for Hari-san, then.

03:46.070 --> 03:46.950
I'll pick this one!

03:47.560 --> 03:48.340
Please give me this one!

03:48.800 --> 03:49.540
Thank you!

03:49.890 --> 03:51.050
Thank you!

03:51.050 --> 03:52.360
I will excuse myself, then!

03:54.450 --> 03:54.840
Huh?

03:55.320 --> 03:56.180
Yancham?

03:56.880 --> 03:58.260
Harimaron's gone, too.

04:07.400 --> 04:07.800
Huh?

04:08.580 --> 04:09.950
Are you alone?

04:10.750 --> 04:11.390
Where's your Trainer?

04:15.200 --> 04:15.940
Could it be...

04:16.560 --> 04:17.200
Are you lost?

04:19.800 --> 04:21.950
Hey, I'll help you search for your friends.

04:23.800 --> 04:24.440
Nice to meet you.

04:25.010 --> 04:25.970
I'm Manon.

04:26.600 --> 04:29.180
You see, my partner is a Harimaron too.

04:29.960 --> 04:31.140
Its name is Hari-san.

04:42.120 --> 04:42.870
Yancham!

04:46.300 --> 04:47.130
Where's Harimaron?

04:49.900 --> 04:51.160
Did you get separated?

04:51.720 --> 04:52.730
This is bad.

04:53.300 --> 04:53.940
Anyway, let's look for it.

05:01.270 --> 05:02.360
There, there.

05:02.800 --> 05:03.340
Huh?

05:04.010 --> 05:04.950
That Harimaron...

05:07.330 --> 05:07.950
I knew it!

05:08.520 --> 05:10.300
Harimaron!

05:10.300 --> 05:11.550
Where are you?

05:11.930 --> 05:12.670
There they are!

05:13.620 --> 05:14.550
Look, over there.

05:17.740 --> 05:18.380
Harimaron!

05:19.040 --> 05:21.310
Geez, where have you been?

05:23.640 --> 05:25.060
Isn't this great, Yancham.

05:49.190 --> 05:53.020
Tierno, Trova, Sana, thanks for finding it.

05:53.320 --> 05:55.030
No, it wasn't us.

05:55.640 --> 05:57.700
It was Manon-san here who did.

06:03.540 --> 06:05.240
Wh-What's the matter?

06:08.190 --> 06:10.810
Sorry, sorry! Did I startle you?

06:19.480 --> 06:20.190
The truth is,

06:21.000 --> 06:23.110
my partner is also a Harimaron.

06:24.120 --> 06:27.610
That's why I couldn't help but remember Hari-san.

06:28.570 --> 06:30.110
You call it Hari-san, huh?

06:30.400 --> 06:30.700
Yeah.

06:31.590 --> 06:33.250
It's the most dependable Pokémon out there, see.

06:34.040 --> 06:37.640
Our Harimaron here is the biggest the biggest lover of Pofflés out there

06:39.880 --> 06:41.090
That's awesome!

06:41.970 --> 06:43.630
You said "remember"...

06:43.630 --> 06:44.920
Isn't it with you right now?

06:46.190 --> 06:46.520
No...

06:48.280 --> 06:50.870
Hari-san has been asleep for a long time...

06:52.560 --> 06:53.480
...and it won't wake up.

06:54.990 --> 06:56.810
Oh... I'm sorry, Manon-chan.

06:57.420 --> 06:58.850
No, it's fine!

06:59.650 --> 07:03.470
So right now, it's getting treatment at a place called the Fleur-de-lis Labs.

07:03.700 --> 07:04.520
I see.

07:06.170 --> 07:07.560
Hey, Satoshi-kun.

07:09.050 --> 07:09.990
Having a strategy meeting?

07:10.880 --> 07:11.880
Professor Platane!

07:12.540 --> 07:13.010
Huh?

07:14.560 --> 07:15.240
Manon-kun!

07:15.640 --> 07:16.210
Professor!

07:16.880 --> 07:17.710
When did you arrive here?

07:18.240 --> 07:19.790
Have you come to root for Alan?

07:21.190 --> 07:21.890
Yeah...

07:23.060 --> 07:23.710
For Alan?

07:26.410 --> 07:27.670
Lizardon, Flamethrower!

07:37.520 --> 07:39.310
Congratulations on making it to the finals.

07:41.190 --> 07:43.800
I guess for you, the finals will be a piece of cake as well, or what do you think?

07:45.130 --> 07:46.150
Don't interfere.

07:46.760 --> 07:47.470
I'm in the middle of preparing.

07:47.920 --> 07:48.600
Right...

07:49.400 --> 07:51.020
I didn't think you'd think enter the Kalos League.

07:51.760 --> 07:55.740
Then again, if you're aspiring to become the strongest, I guess it's no wonder.

07:56.710 --> 07:58.780
This fight has nothing to do with being the strongest.

08:00.220 --> 08:00.570
I just...

08:01.320 --> 08:02.170
...wanted to fight...

08:02.950 --> 08:03.280
...him.

08:04.380 --> 08:05.460
You mean Satoshi?

08:07.280 --> 08:08.760
The fact that you think about him so much...

08:09.110 --> 08:10.140
...must make him happy.

08:10.580 --> 08:11.530
What are you trying to say?

08:12.680 --> 08:13.380
What about you?

08:13.890 --> 08:15.280
Which of your faces is the real you?

08:19.390 --> 08:23.020
It seems you'll soon be done collecting Mega Evolution energy, too.

08:24.350 --> 08:25.990
Once you've saved Harimaron...

08:26.440 --> 08:27.280
...what will you do next?

08:39.860 --> 08:41.210
It's none of your business.

08:43.580 --> 08:44.220
You're right.

08:50.550 --> 08:51.220
Hey...

08:51.710 --> 08:53.640
We're done for today, right?

08:54.040 --> 08:55.390
I'm hungry...

08:59.470 --> 09:00.390
Don't talk!

09:01.050 --> 09:03.240
All right, let's go back and start editing!

09:03.240 --> 09:04.510
What?

09:04.870 --> 09:06.710
We aren't done yet?

09:06.710 --> 09:09.120
We won't make it in time for the broadcast!

09:09.370 --> 09:11.150
Come on, let's work! Work!

09:11.930 --> 09:13.610
Right.

09:16.540 --> 09:18.440
Oh, just look forward to tomorrow.

09:19.080 --> 09:20.850
We'll give you some big news.

09:21.480 --> 09:26.320
The Pokémon that are still around now that we've reached the finals possess strength and have undergone a careful screening process.

09:27.230 --> 09:29.340
So our plan is to round them all up in one fell swoop!

09:30.440 --> 09:31.380
Quiet!

09:33.650 --> 09:35.080
Have you met Alan already?

09:35.650 --> 09:36.200
No.

09:37.130 --> 09:38.740
I'm fine with waiting until the finals are over.

09:39.700 --> 09:41.240
I'm sure he's focusing right now.

09:41.760 --> 09:42.960
I don't want to get in the way.

09:44.340 --> 09:46.150
I'm planning on meeting him after the finals.

09:46.920 --> 09:47.530
I see.

09:48.930 --> 09:50.980
By the way, Professor, what brings you here?

09:51.820 --> 09:53.720
You know that power of Gekkouga's?

09:54.600 --> 09:56.640
There are some things I've found out about it.

09:59.200 --> 09:59.840
Pokémon...

10:00.020 --> 10:01.000
...Quiz!

10:01.290 --> 10:02.410
The answer is...?

10:03.980 --> 10:13.990
Coming up next:

10:03.980 --> 10:08.950
The secret behind Satoshi Gekkouga?

10:04.950 --> 10:09.680
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

10:08.980 --> 10:13.990
Satoshi and Fleur-de-lis are...!?

10:28.290 --> 10:29.500
Drain Punch, huh...?

10:32.330 --> 10:35.190
It is an amazing punch that absorbs the opponent's power.

10:36.750 --> 10:38.550
If you use Leech Seed on top of that,

10:39.230 --> 10:41.920
you might be able to make the battle advance in your advantage.

10:43.810 --> 10:45.020
It really is amazing.

10:46.160 --> 10:48.460
There are so many fighting styles I do not know about.

10:49.350 --> 10:51.010
The world is still so wide.

10:52.230 --> 10:54.460
Pokémon battles are deep.

10:57.090 --> 10:59.440
Having been able to battle Satoshi in this tournament...

11:00.000 --> 11:02.950
...has been a great experience for me, I am sure.

11:04.590 --> 11:05.960
I have never had...

11:06.920 --> 11:07.840
...such a fun battle.

11:09.570 --> 11:09.980
But...

11:10.590 --> 11:12.260
...challenging the Kalos League...

11:13.030 --> 11:14.190
...is over for me.

11:17.960 --> 11:18.760
I cheered Satoshi on...

11:19.370 --> 11:20.960
...with a smile, but...

11:22.270 --> 11:22.820
...in the end...

11:24.110 --> 11:25.050
I cannot help but...

11:25.870 --> 11:27.000
...feel disappointed.

11:29.080 --> 11:30.360
I would have liked to...

11:31.040 --> 11:32.160
...have many more battles here.

11:37.390 --> 11:37.970
I have to...

11:39.030 --> 11:40.520
I have to get a lot more experience!

11:41.380 --> 11:43.100
I do not have enough time to cry.

11:46.810 --> 11:48.550
What do you think, Fleur-de-lis-sama?

11:49.520 --> 11:53.020
You will watch tomorrow's finals from here.

11:53.730 --> 11:57.070
Thank you for responding to my sudden request.

11:57.410 --> 12:03.240
Don't mention it; all parties involved are grateful that a Kalos celebrity will watch the match.

12:06.410 --> 12:11.050
All right, I will excuse myself now. If you need anything, please call me.

12:14.460 --> 12:15.320
Fleur-de-lis-sama.

12:28.970 --> 12:30.860
We've brought the center of Miare under our control.

12:32.150 --> 12:33.940
The Gym is closed during the tournament,

12:34.560 --> 12:35.670
so it was easy.

12:36.020 --> 12:38.050
As soon as the preparations are done, report to me.

12:38.450 --> 12:39.490
Understood.

12:41.350 --> 12:42.750
How's Manon doing?

12:42.750 --> 12:44.230
She is in the Trainer village.

12:44.540 --> 12:46.660
She is in contact with the opponent in the finals.

12:47.820 --> 12:48.180
Oh...

12:48.990 --> 12:50.970
That Gekkouga Trainer, huh?

12:52.280 --> 12:56.140
These old documents have records of a similar case.

12:57.030 --> 12:57.680
It's called...

12:58.060 --> 12:58.880
...a "bond phenomenon".

12:59.640 --> 13:00.870
"Bond phenomenon"...

13:02.670 --> 13:09.730
According to these documents, it occurs when the trust between Trainer and Pokémon is strong, but only very rarely.

13:10.720 --> 13:15.230
It also appears the Pokémon's own latent powers plays a role.

13:16.360 --> 13:18.710
It doesn't seem it occurs with just any Pokémon.

13:20.040 --> 13:21.950
So it doesn't happen to everyone.

13:22.640 --> 13:26.030
I've said before that Gekkouga chose Satoshi-kun.

13:27.000 --> 13:31.640
It may have sensed its latent powers from the beginning,

13:32.810 --> 13:36.340
...and that you specifically would be able to draw out its power.

13:37.640 --> 13:40.820
Your meeting may have been inevitable.

13:42.670 --> 13:43.100
Yes.

13:44.430 --> 13:45.640
Hurry with the setup.

13:46.360 --> 13:46.540
Roger!

13:46.590 --> 13:46.740
Roger!

14:14.570 --> 14:16.100
I'll be fine from now on.

14:16.540 --> 14:17.800
You should stay here overnight.

14:18.120 --> 14:19.340
I want to talk to you more!

14:19.890 --> 14:20.260
Me too!

14:20.860 --> 14:22.790
But Fleur-de-lis-san is waiting...

14:23.040 --> 14:25.340
Also, it'd be bad if I ran into Alan, so...

14:26.480 --> 14:28.200
Harimaron, thank you.

14:28.620 --> 14:29.860
I'm glad I met you guys.

14:35.370 --> 14:39.160
Unlike my Hari-san, this Harimaron always makes a fool of itself.

14:39.620 --> 14:40.690
You're like me!

14:43.240 --> 14:44.190
Hey, Manon-chan.

14:45.660 --> 14:47.850
Please tell us if there's something we can do.

14:48.620 --> 14:49.900
We'll help you with anything.

14:50.360 --> 14:52.210
Yeah! That's right, that's right!

14:52.840 --> 14:53.220
Okay.

14:54.520 --> 14:56.710
I hope Hari-san gets better soon.

14:57.990 --> 14:59.300
Hari-san will be fine.

14:59.780 --> 15:01.960
It'll get better, I just know it.

15:02.990 --> 15:07.350
When it gets better, let's have our Harimaron and your Hari-san play together!

15:08.650 --> 15:10.010
Thank you, Serena,

15:10.010 --> 15:10.600
Eureka!

15:11.060 --> 15:11.750
I'm off, then.

15:13.890 --> 15:15.000
Today was fun!

15:15.340 --> 15:16.580
Let's meet again tomorrow!

15:16.800 --> 15:17.140
Yeah!

15:22.040 --> 15:23.360
It's finally time for the match against Alan.

15:24.210 --> 15:25.880
Now that we've made it this far, we can only think about one thing:

15:26.750 --> 15:28.150
We'll battle better than ever before...

15:29.000 --> 15:29.360
...and win!

15:39.280 --> 15:40.930
Tomorrow we'll battle Satoshi.

15:41.920 --> 15:43.340
I'm really looking forward to that.

15:43.980 --> 15:44.820
I wonder what's going on with me.

15:45.780 --> 15:47.090
I genuinely feel that way.

16:00.090 --> 16:00.900
Lizardon...

16:01.600 --> 16:02.150
Just a bit more.

16:03.280 --> 16:04.650
Just a bit more, and we'll have collected enough.

16:16.620 --> 16:17.000
Hey.

16:17.440 --> 16:18.330
You're Satoshi-kun, right?

16:18.810 --> 16:19.320
Yes.

16:19.860 --> 16:20.420
Who are you?

16:21.280 --> 16:23.140
My name is Fleur-de-lis.

16:23.980 --> 16:24.230
Oh,

16:25.210 --> 16:26.050
Manon mentioned you.

16:26.690 --> 16:28.710
Oh, I didn't know you knew Manon.

16:29.120 --> 16:31.270
Yeah, I do. We were with her just a moment ago.

16:31.630 --> 16:33.110
If you were looking for her, she's just gone to the hotel.

16:33.320 --> 16:35.060
The one I want to talk to is you.

16:35.420 --> 16:36.480
Huh? Me?

16:38.280 --> 16:39.800
Can we talk for a bit?

16:41.480 --> 16:42.330
Lizardon...

16:42.760 --> 16:43.990
You've become strong.

16:51.980 --> 16:53.030
Oh shoot.

16:55.130 --> 16:56.930
There were many things I wanted to talk to you about,

16:58.510 --> 17:00.740
but I can't manage to put it into words.

17:02.360 --> 17:03.540
Are you angry...

17:04.370 --> 17:05.020
...that I didn't come back?

17:05.680 --> 17:06.040
No.

17:06.630 --> 17:07.160
I heard...

17:07.920 --> 17:10.300
...that you assist Fleur-de-lis-san with his work.

17:11.160 --> 17:11.570
I can't...

17:12.410 --> 17:14.540
...expose you to any danger.

17:16.360 --> 17:18.450
The energy emitted during Mega Evolution...

17:19.120 --> 17:20.890
...is said to be of great value.

17:21.660 --> 17:22.860
There are people who would do anything...

17:23.560 --> 17:25.440
...to abuse that power.

17:26.150 --> 17:28.620
So you distanced yourself from me for my own sake?

17:30.650 --> 17:31.880
I can't go back right now.

17:33.160 --> 17:34.360
I've lost even more now than...

17:34.900 --> 17:36.200
...I had before I set off on my journey.

17:37.430 --> 17:38.730
Until I get it back...

17:40.420 --> 17:41.240
That's another reason why I...

17:41.950 --> 17:43.090
...have to get much stronger.

17:46.030 --> 17:47.350
You should do as you please.

17:50.160 --> 17:54.130
You and your Gekkouga are all people talk about in this tournament.

17:55.290 --> 17:56.760
Do you mean the bond phenomenon?

17:57.330 --> 17:57.790
Oh...

17:58.200 --> 17:59.240
"Bond phenomenon", huh...?

17:59.740 --> 18:00.120
Yes.

18:00.630 --> 18:02.520
Professor Platane researched it for us.

18:03.110 --> 18:03.590
And so...

18:04.800 --> 18:06.320
That power is excellent.

18:06.920 --> 18:08.900
This is all new potential for Pokémon and humans.

18:09.780 --> 18:12.600
It might guide us toward the world of the future.

18:14.090 --> 18:19.320
I have a strong interest in Mega Evolution and the bond between people and Pokémon, you see.

18:20.120 --> 18:23.170
Once the League is over, please tell me more about it.

18:24.250 --> 18:25.560
Will you promise me?

18:26.580 --> 18:27.500
Uh-huh...

18:27.920 --> 18:28.500
Thank you.

18:29.380 --> 18:29.820
Well then,

18:30.320 --> 18:31.810
do your best in the finals.

18:32.390 --> 18:32.800
I will.

18:52.010 --> 18:52.940
Fleur-de-lis-san!

18:53.880 --> 18:54.340
Manon,

18:55.150 --> 18:56.020
I've got good news.

18:56.540 --> 18:56.820
Huh?

18:57.400 --> 18:58.040
Tomorrow,

18:58.600 --> 19:00.030
everything will be fine.

19:00.450 --> 19:01.220
Harimaron too...

19:01.940 --> 19:04.800
All thanks to Alan collecting Mega Evolution energy.

19:07.290 --> 19:08.160
Thank goodness.

19:09.400 --> 19:10.640
I'm so happy.

19:18.530 --> 19:22.320
Heated fights have unfolded at the Kalos League Miare Tournament.

19:22.320 --> 19:26.250
At last, the time for the final decisive match has come.

19:39.640 --> 19:41.360
All of Kalos' attention is on this match.

19:41.850 --> 19:43.230
Who will be standing at the top?

19:44.390 --> 19:45.240
Satoshi...

19:46.700 --> 19:47.520
...or Alan?

19:56.960 --> 19:58.540
Both competitors are entering the stadium!

20:15.150 --> 20:15.620
The next episode...

20:16.380 --> 20:17.140
...will finally be...

20:18.070 --> 20:20.630
...the climax of the Kalos League!

20:26.110 --> 20:28.290
The passionate and exciting points of the Pokémon movie!

20:28.530 --> 20:29.590
Get blown away!

20:30.970 --> 21:21.040
The blockbuster is
currently in theaters!

20:30.970 --> 20:33.790
MAGEARNA

20:31.160 --> 20:36.580
Magearna protects injured Pokémon at the Nebel Plateau together with Volcanion.

20:37.030 --> 20:38.620
It is caring and has a strong character.

20:39.290 --> 20:39.800
However...

20:42.720 --> 20:44.300
It also has a cute side...

20:44.570 --> 20:46.300
It was quite heavy, was it not?

20:47.680 --> 20:49.120
You made it self-conscious.

20:49.120 --> 20:51.120
What? I am sorry!

20:51.500 --> 20:54.430
Magearna was born 500 years ago.

20:55.270 --> 20:56.900
Your soul...

20:57.370 --> 20:59.980
...will be the stronghold that will protect the people of this country.

21:00.940 --> 21:03.480
Magearna was created in the hope for peace.

21:03.880 --> 21:10.340
However, the power of the Soul Heart dwelling within its heart brought about wars, causing it to disappear.

21:10.600 --> 21:11.720
I'm sorry...

21:12.920 --> 21:13.560
...I was unable to protect you.

21:14.470 --> 21:17.110
What is the true power hidden within Magearna?

21:17.730 --> 21:19.980
This summer, get blown away to the theater!

21:21.040 --> 21:26.050
